※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 7026 LANG_MACRO_ARGUMENT_COUNT

※ A macro written as a function takes the pieces written between the marks, one per
※ parameter.  A macro written as rules says how many by what its patterns match, and
※ answers a different message where none of them does.

macro pair(a: syntax, b: syntax) → syntax:
    ⌜$a⌝

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(pair⌜1u8⌝, ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
